  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Citizen Participation in Devolved Governance and Conflict Prevention</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist in advocating national governance and conflict management in Kenya. 

Catholic Justice &amp; Peace Commission (CJPC) as a national office has purposed to use the national level structures of the Bishops and parliamentary liaison desk for national advocacy on governance and conflict management; and diocesan structures for advocacy on county governance and conflict management at the county level.

National office &#x2013; will focus on capacity strengthening of dioceses in advocacy and technical support, bishops&#x2019; capacity strengthening, national inter-religious forums, policy advocacy, and engagement with parliament and county assemblies. 

Some of the key outcomes from cooperating with the CJPC will include ensuring that the poor have an equal voice in the decision making process, both at a local level and national level. As well ensuring that the Church represents the poor effectively at all levels of society and facilitates meaningful relationships with decision makers at all levels.</narrative>
  </description>
